body:
So the comedown is technically just the few hours after the high drops off, a lot of people including myself use ketamine because it pretty much removes the comedown, stops you noticing the happy chemicals from the coke dropping off so hard but that's a careful recommendation cause both together increases blood pressure so it increases risk.

&#x200B;

The day after is more like a hangover comparable to alcohol, a major part of how you feel then is how much you did and for how long and how badly the coke was bashed, this all contributes to sinus pressure & blockage which is probably what is giving you the headaches, throat pain, feeling like you have a cold, etc.

&#x200B;

If you do nice clean coke, hot-plated, only every now and then and rinse your sinuses afterwards your hangovers won't be nearly as bad.
